<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE dictionary SYSTEM "file://localhost/System/Library/DTDs/sdef.dtd">
<!--
  Soft Return's AppleScript dictionary.

  This file IS the ruled dictionary in docs/AppleScript-Dictionary.md — the vocabulary
  was proposed and ruled on BEFORE this was written (Jon, 2026-08-07/08: ws5plus one
  word, sawyer stays the public preset name, layout JSON included for full CLI parity).
  Every class, verb, parameter, and enumeration below is that document made concrete;
  see it for the "why" behind each shape. The three acceptance scripts at the bottom of
  that doc are the bar this dictionary is meant to clear.

  Every command routes through SoftReturn.Operations.DocumentOperations — the same
  headless layer the CLI (`sr`) and the App Intents (Shortcuts) surfaces call — so the
  three surfaces cannot drift apart. No conversion/diagnosis logic lives in the Cocoa
  Scripting glue itself.

  Job 147 (2026-08-09): the Standard Suite below is declared INLINE, copied verbatim
  from docs/reference/spotlight-schemas/skim.sdef's own Standard Suite (`<cocoa
  name="NSCoreSuite"/>`) instead of `xi:include`-ing CocoaStandard.sdef. This exists to
  test the surviving hypothesis for the -1708 "doesn't understand" bug (jobs 143/144):
  that the runtime NSScriptSuiteRegistry loader in the sandboxed Release process does
  not resolve xi:include the way terminology tooling (sdp/osacompile) does. Unlike the
  old xi:include (which used an xpointer filter to DROP "save"/"delete"/"make" — "Soft
  Return is a viewer"), this inline copy includes those terms because that is what
  Skim's shipping suite actually contains and the point of this experiment is a faithful
  structural copy, not a re-litigation of viewer semantics. SoftReturn.WSDocument does
  not override handleSaveScriptCommand:/NSCreateCommand/NSDeleteCommand, so those verbs
  now compile and dispatch through AppKit's own default NSDocument/NSApplication
  behavior rather than being absent from the dictionary — flagged here, not silently
  shipped; see the job 147 report for the product-behavior call this raises for Jon.
-->
<dictionary title="Soft Return Terminology">
    <suite name="Standard Suite" code="core"
           description="Common classes and commands for all applications.">

        <cocoa name="NSCoreSuite"/>

        <command name="open" code="aevtodoc" description="Open a document.">
            <direct-parameter description="The file(s) to be opened.">
                <type type="file"/>
                <type type="file" list="yes"/>
            </direct-parameter>
            <result description="The opened document(s).">
                <type type="document"/>
                <type type="document" list="yes"/>
            </result>
        </command>

        <enumeration name="save options" code="savo">
            <enumerator name="yes" code="yes " description="Save the file."/>
            <enumerator name="no" code="no  " description="Do not save the file."/>
            <enumerator name="ask" code="ask " description="Ask the user whether or not to save the file."/>
        </enumeration>

        <command name="close" code="coreclos" description="Close a document.">
            <cocoa class="NSCloseCommand"/>
            <direct-parameter type="specifier" description="the document(s) or window(s) to close."/>
            <parameter name="saving" code="savo" type="save options" optional="yes" description="Should changes be saved before closing?">
                <cocoa key="SaveOptions"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="saving in" code="kfil" type="file" optional="yes" description="The file in which to save the document, if so.">
                <cocoa key="File"/>
            </parameter>
        </command>

        <command name="save" code="coresave" description="Save a document.">
            <direct-parameter type="specifier" description="The document(s) or window(s) to save."/>
            <parameter name="in" code="kfil" type="file" optional="yes" description="The file in which to save the document.">
                <cocoa key="File"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="as" code="fltp" type="text" optional="yes" description="The file format to use. Should be one of &quot;PDF&quot;, &quot;PDF Bundle&quot;, &quot;PDF Without Notes&quot;, &quot;PDF With Embedded Notes&quot;, &quot;PostScript&quot;, &quot;PostScript Without Notes&quot;, &quot;Encapsulated PostScript&quot;, &quot;Encapsulated PostScript Without Notes&quot;, &quot;DVI&quot;, &quot;DVI Without Notes&quot;, &quot;XDV&quot;, &quot;XDV Without Notes&quot;, &quot;Skim Notes&quot;, &quot;Notes as Text&quot;, &quot;Notes as RTF&quot;, &quot;Notes as RTFD&quot;, and &quot;Notes as FDF&quot;, or the name of a custom export template.">
                <cocoa key="FileType"/>
            </parameter>
        </command>

        <enumeration name="printing error handling" code="enum">
            <enumerator name="standard" code="lwst" description="Standard PostScript error handling">
                <cocoa boolean-value="NO"/>
            </enumerator>
            <enumerator name="detailed" code="lwdt" description="print a detailed report of PostScript errors">
                <cocoa boolean-value="YES"/>
            </enumerator>
        </enumeration>

        <record-type name="print settings" code="pset">
            <property name="copies" code="lwcp" type="integer" description="the number of copies of a document to be printed">
                <cocoa key="NSCopies"/>
            </property>
            <property name="collating" code="lwcl" type="boolean" description="Should printed copies be collated?">
                <cocoa key="NSMustCollate"/>
            </property>
            <property name="starting page" code="lwfp" type="integer" description="the first page of the document to be printed">
                <cocoa key="NSFirstPage"/>
            </property>
            <property name="ending page" code="lwlp" type="integer" description="the last page of the document to be printed">
                <cocoa key="NSLastPage"/>
            </property>
            <property name="pages across" code="lwla" type="integer" description="number of logical pages laid across a physical page">
                <cocoa key="NSPagesAcross"/>
            </property>
            <property name="pages down" code="lwld" type="integer" description="number of logical pages laid out down a physical page">
                <cocoa key="NSPagesDown"/>
            </property>
            <property name="requested print time" code="lwqt" type="date" description="the time at which the desktop printer should print the document">
                <cocoa key="NSPrintTime"/>
            </property>
            <property name="error handling" code="lweh" type="printing error handling" description="how errors are handled">
                <cocoa key="NSDetailedErrorReporting"/>
            </property>
            <property name="fax number" code="faxn" type="text" description="for fax number">
                <cocoa key="NSFaxNumber"/>
            </property>
            <property name="target printer" code="trpr" type="text" description="for target printer">
                <cocoa key="NSPrinterName"/>
            </property>
        </record-type>

        <command name="print" code="aevtpdoc" description="Print a document.">
            <direct-parameter description="The file(s), document(s), or window(s) to be printed.">
                <type type="file" list="yes"/>
                <type type="specifier"/>
            </direct-parameter>
            <parameter name="with properties" code="prdt" type="print settings" optional="yes" description="The print settings to use.">
                <cocoa key="PrintSettings"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="print dialog" code="pdlg" type="boolean" optional="yes" description="Should the application show the print dialog?">
                <cocoa key="ShowPrintDialog"/>
            </parameter>
        </command>

        <command name="quit" code="aevtquit" description="Quit the application.">
            <cocoa class="NSQuitCommand"/>
            <parameter name="saving" code="savo" type="save options" optional="yes" description="Should changes be saved before quitting?">
                <cocoa key="SaveOptions"/>
            </parameter>
        </command>

        <command name="count" code="corecnte" description="Return the number of elements of a particular class within an object.">
            <cocoa class="NSCountCommand"/>
            <direct-parameter type="specifier" description="The objects to be counted."/>
            <parameter name="each" code="kocl" type="type" optional="yes" description="The class of objects to be counted." hidden="yes">
                <cocoa key="ObjectClass"/>
            </parameter>
            <result type="integer" description="The count."/>
        </command>

        <command name="delete" code="coredelo" description="Delete an object.">
            <cocoa class="NSDeleteCommand"/>
            <direct-parameter type="specifier" description="The object(s) to delete."/>
        </command>

        <command name="duplicate" code="coreclon" description="Copy an object.">
            <cocoa class="NSCloneCommand"/>
            <direct-parameter type="specifier" description="The object(s) to copy."/>
            <parameter name="to" code="insh" type="location specifier" description="The location for the new copy or copies." optional="yes">
                <cocoa key="ToLocation"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="with properties" code="prdt" type="record" description="Properties to set in the new copy or copies right away." optional="yes">
                <cocoa key="WithProperties"/>
            </parameter>
        </command>

        <command name="exists" code="coredoex" description="Verify that an object exists.">
            <cocoa class="NSExistsCommand"/>
            <direct-parameter type="any" description="The object(s) to check."/>
            <result type="boolean" description="Did the object(s) exist?"/>
        </command>

        <command name="make" code="corecrel" description="Create a new object.">
            <cocoa class="NSCreateCommand"/>
            <parameter name="new" code="kocl" type="type" description="The class of the new object.">
                <cocoa key="ObjectClass"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="at" code="insh" type="location specifier" optional="yes" description="The location at which to insert the object.">
                <cocoa key="Location"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="with data" code="data" type="any" optional="yes" description="The initial contents of the object.">
                <cocoa key="ObjectData"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="with properties" code="prdt" type="record" optional="yes" description="The initial values for properties of the object.">
                <cocoa key="KeyDictionary"/>
            </parameter>
            <result type="specifier" description="The new object."/>
        </command>

        <command name="move" code="coremove" description="Move an object to a new location.">
            <cocoa class="NSMoveCommand"/>
            <direct-parameter type="specifier" description="The object(s) to move."/>
            <parameter name="to" code="insh" type="location specifier" description="The new location for the object(s).">
                <cocoa key="ToLocation"/>
            </parameter>
        </command>

        <class name="application" code="capp"
               description="The application's top level scripting object.">
            <cocoa class="NSApplication"/>
            <property name="name" code="pnam" type="text" access="r" description="The name of the application."/>
            <property name="frontmost" code="pisf" type="boolean" access="r" description="Is this the active application?">
                <cocoa key="isActive"/>
            </property>
            <property name="version" code="vers" type="text" access="r" description="The version number of the application."/>
            <element type="document">
                <cocoa key="orderedDocuments"/>
            </element>
            <element type="window" access="r">
                <cocoa key="orderedWindows"/>
            </element>
            <responds-to command="open">
                <cocoa method="handleOpenScriptCommand:"/>
            </responds-to>
            <responds-to command="print">
                <cocoa method="handlePrintScriptCommand:"/>
            </responds-to>
            <responds-to command="quit">
                <cocoa method="handleQuitScriptCommand:"/>
            </responds-to>
        </class>

        <class name="document" code="docu"
               description="A document.">
            <cocoa class="NSDocument"/>
            <property name="name" code="pnam" type="text" access="r" description="Its name.">
                <cocoa key="displayName"/>
            </property>
            <property name="modified" code="imod" type="boolean" access="r" description="Has it been modified since the last save?">
                <cocoa key="isDocumentEdited"/>
            </property>
            <property name="file" code="file" type="file" access="r" description="Its location on disk, if it has one.">
                <cocoa key="fileURL"/>
            </property>
            <property name="path" code="ppth" type="text" access="r" hidden="yes"
                       description="The document's path.">
                <cocoa key="fileName"/>
            </property>
            <responds-to command="close">
                <cocoa method="handleCloseScriptCommand:"/>
            </responds-to>
            <responds-to command="print">
                <cocoa method="handlePrintScriptCommand:"/>
            </responds-to>
            <responds-to command="save">
                <cocoa method="handleSaveScriptCommand:"/>
            </responds-to>
        </class>

        <class name="window" code="cwin"
               description="A window.">
            <cocoa class="NSWindow"/>
            <property name="name" code="pnam" type="text" access="r" description="The title of the window.">
                <cocoa key="title"/>
            </property>
            <property name="id" code="ID  " type="integer" access="r" description="The unique identifier of the window.">
                <cocoa key="uniqueID"/>
            </property>
            <property name="index" code="pidx" type="integer" description="The index of the window, ordered front to back.">
                <cocoa key="orderedIndex"/>
            </property>
            <property name="bounds" code="pbnd" type="rectangle" description="The bounding rectangle of the window.">
                <cocoa key="boundsAsQDRect"/>
            </property>
            <property name="closeable" code="hclb" type="boolean" access="r" description="Does the window have a close button?">
                <cocoa key="hasCloseBox"/>
            </property>
            <property name="miniaturizable" code="ismn" type="boolean" access="r" description="Does the window have a minimize button?">
                <cocoa key="isMiniaturizable"/>
            </property>
            <property name="miniaturized" code="pmnd" type="boolean" description="Is the window minimized right now?">
                <cocoa key="isMiniaturized"/>
            </property>
            <property name="resizable" code="prsz" type="boolean" access="r" description="Can the window be resized?">
                <cocoa key="isResizable"/>
            </property>
            <property name="visible" code="pvis" type="boolean" description="Is the window visible right now?">
                <cocoa key="isVisible"/>
            </property>
            <property name="zoomable" code="iszm" type="boolean" access="r" description="Does the window have a zoom button?">
                <cocoa key="isZoomable"/>
            </property>
            <property name="zoomed" code="pzum" type="boolean" description="Is the window zoomed right now?">
                <cocoa key="isZoomed"/>
            </property>
            <property name="document" code="docu" type="document" access="r" description="The document whose contents are displayed in the window."/>
            <responds-to command="close">
                <cocoa method="handleCloseScriptCommand:"/>
            </responds-to>
            <responds-to command="print">
                <cocoa method="handlePrintScriptCommand:"/>
            </responds-to>
            <responds-to command="save">
                <cocoa method="handleSaveScriptCommand:"/>
            </responds-to>
        </class>

    </suite>

    <suite name="Soft Return Suite" code="SRsu"
           description="Classes and commands specific to Soft Return: converting, diagnosing, and reading WordStar-era documents.">

        <!-- ============================== Enumerations ============================== -->

        <enumeration name="variant" code="SRva"
                     description="Which WordStar-era format a document was written in — the CLI's --variant.">
            <enumerator name="ws4" code="SRv4" description="WordStar 4 through 6."/>
            <enumerator name="ws5plus" code="SRv5" description="WordStar 5 through 7 (the CLI's ws5+)."/>
            <enumerator name="printstream" code="SRvp" description="A print-to-disk capture."/>
            <enumerator name="text" code="SRvt" description="Plain text, no WordStar formatting."/>
        </enumeration>

        <enumeration name="style" code="SRsy"
                     description="How a document is rendered — the CLI's --mode, plus the app's own on-screen Native view (job 313B, superseding an earlier &quot;Native has no export equivalent&quot; ruling). Exporting/converting as native only changes PDF output — every other format is identical to printed.">
            <enumerator name="native" code="SRsn" description="The window's own AppKit-rendered facsimile (Courier Prime, title faces). PDF export/convert reuses the exact print-path render Cmd-P uses; every other format is identical to printed."/>
            <enumerator name="printed" code="SRsp" description="Line-for-line, the 1990 facsimile — the engine's own literal PDF bytes."/>
            <enumerator name="modern" code="SRsm" description="Reflowed for a modern audience."/>
        </enumeration>

        <enumeration name="export format" code="SRfm"
                     description="An output format export/convert can produce — the CLI's -t/--to, full parity including layout JSON.">
            <enumerator name="plain text" code="SRft" description="The library's text emitter."/>
            <enumerator name="Markdown" code="SRfk" description="The library's markdown emitter."/>
            <enumerator name="HTML" code="SRfh" description="The library's html emitter."/>
            <enumerator name="RTF" code="SRfr" description="The library's rtf emitter."/>
            <enumerator name="PDF" code="SRfp" description="The library's pdf emitter."/>
            <enumerator name="layout JSON" code="SRfj"
                       description="The full viewer contract as JSON — the CLI's -t layout."/>
        </enumeration>

        <enumeration name="note reference style" code="SRnr"
                     description="How note references are marked in Modern output — the CLI's --note-refs.">
            <enumerator name="word style" code="SRnw"
                       description="Arabic footnotes, lowercase-roman endnotes, WordStar tags for annotations."/>
            <enumerator name="prefixed" code="SRnp"
                       description="footnote 1 2 3, endnote e1 e2, annotation a1 a2 — matched across formats."/>
        </enumeration>

        <enumeration name="page size" code="SRpz"
                     description="A named printed-sheet override.">
            <enumerator name="US letter" code="SRpl"/>
            <enumerator name="US legal" code="SRpg"/>
            <enumerator name="A4" code="SRp4"/>
        </enumeration>

        <enumeration name="settings preset" code="SRpr"
                     description="A named page-settings preset — the CLI's --page-settings preset names.">
            <enumerator name="factory" code="SRxf"
                       description="WordStar's own factory geometry (the CLI's 'default')."/>
            <enumerator name="sawyer" code="SRxs"
                       description="Robert J. Sawyer's WSCHANGE-recovered machine."/>
            <enumerator name="modern" code="SRxm"
                       description="Modern style's own 1in-margin page (the CLI's 'modern')."/>
        </enumeration>

        <enumeration name="pictures mode" code="SRpx"
                     description="Job 373 (b24 FLAG UI): how .PIX image references are handled — the CLI's --pictures {off,embed,export}.">
            <enumerator name="off" code="SRxo" description="The plain [image: NAME] placeholder, no picture handling."/>
            <enumerator name="embed" code="SRxe" description="RTF/PDF native embedding, HTML data URI, MD exports files. The default."/>
            <enumerator name="export" code="SRxx" description="PNG files beside the output, relative links from HTML/MD; RTF/PDF still embed."/>
        </enumeration>

        <enumeration name="fonts" code="SRfn"
                     description="Job 504: which importer the RTF font names are chosen for — the CLI's --fonts, CtrlKD.FontsTarget.">
            <enumerator name="office" code="SRof" description="Word AND Google Docs both resolve the Microsoft names — the widest single answer."/>
            <enumerator name="mac" code="SRmc" description="Cocoa-native names — TextEdit/Pages/Soft Return.app world. The default here (the CLI's own D7 ruling: sr is the Mac tool)."/>
            <enumerator name="google" code="SRgg" description="Google Docs' own catalog where it has something Office lacks."/>
            <enumerator name="linux" code="SRlx" description="The URW base-35 clones — free, metric-compatible copies of this era's fonts."/>
        </enumeration>

        <enumeration name="page numbers mode" code="SRpn"
                     description="Job 506 (b31): WordStar's own AUTOMATIC page number — the CLI's --page-numbers {auto,on,off}. Printed PDF only.">
            <enumerator name="auto" code="SRpa" description="The document's own dot commands decide — .pn/.pg turn it on, .op turns it off. A document that never touches any of them gets no number. The default."/>
            <enumerator name="on" code="SRpo" description="Force stock default numbering (bottom row a footer would use; .pc repositions it) even on a silent document."/>
            <enumerator name="off" code="SRp0" description="Suppress it unconditionally."/>
        </enumeration>

        <enumeration name="sentence spacing mode" code="SRsq"
                     description="Job 521 (N9, b33): the typewriter double space after a sentence-ending . ? or ! — the CLI's --sentence-spacing {auto,keep,single}.">
            <enumerator name="auto" code="SRsa" description="Modern exports collapse it to a single space; Printed and Native exports keep the document exactly as authored. The default."/>
            <enumerator name="keep" code="SRsk" description="Keep the document's own spacing exactly as authored, regardless of style."/>
            <enumerator name="single" code="SRsl" description="Collapse it to a single space, regardless of style."/>
        </enumeration>

        <enumeration name="zoom setting" code="SRzs"
                     description="A named zoom state; a zoom can also be a plain percentage number.">
            <enumerator name="fit" code="SRzf" description="Scaled to fill the window."/>
            <enumerator name="actual size" code="SRza" description="100% — true size against a ruler."/>
        </enumeration>

        <!-- ================================ Records ================================ -->

        <record-type name="page settings" code="SRrp"
                     description="Replacement page geometry — the CLI's PageSettings, one field per dot command it can override. Every field is optional; an absent field leaves the document's own (or the factory) value alone.">
            <property name="margin top" code="SRr1" type="real" description="`.mt` replacement, in lines at 6 LPI.">
                <cocoa key="marginTop"/>
            </property>
            <property name="margin bottom" code="SRr2" type="real" description="`.mb` replacement, in lines at 6 LPI.">
                <cocoa key="marginBottom"/>
            </property>
            <property name="page offset" code="SRr3" type="real" description="`.po` replacement, in columns at 10 CPI.">
                <cocoa key="pageOffset"/>
            </property>
            <property name="header margin" code="SRr4" type="real" description="`.hm` replacement, in lines at 6 LPI.">
                <cocoa key="headerMargin"/>
            </property>
            <property name="footer margin" code="SRr5" type="real" description="`.fm` replacement, in lines at 6 LPI.">
                <cocoa key="footerMargin"/>
            </property>
            <property name="paper size" code="SRr7" type="page size" description="Job 504: a named sheet size (US letter/US legal/A4), the CLI's --page-settings size=. Sets page length via the library's own size table — an explicit page length in the same record wins if both are given.">
                <cocoa key="paperSize"/>
            </property>
            <property name="page length" code="SRr6" type="real" description="`.pl` replacement, in lines at 6 LPI.">
                <cocoa key="pageLength"/>
            </property>
        </record-type>

        <record-type name="conversion result" code="SRrc"
                     description="What a batch convert did — the CLI's -d batch summary.">
            <property name="converted" code="SRc1" type="integer" description="Files that produced at least one output.">
                <cocoa key="converted"/>
            </property>
            <property name="skipped" code="SRc2" type="integer" description="Files that were not convertible WordStar-era documents.">
                <cocoa key="skipped"/>
            </property>
            <property name="failed" code="SRc3" type="file" list="yes" description="Files that failed for some other reason.">
                <cocoa key="failed"/>
            </property>
        </record-type>

        <record-type name="diagnosis" code="SRrd"
                     description="What a file IS — the CLI's --diagnose, as a record instead of JSON.">
            <property name="variant" code="SRd1" type="variant" description="The detected variant.">
                <cocoa key="variant"/>
            </property>
            <property name="pages" code="SRd2" type="integer"
                      description="Printed pagination; missing only when the bytes did not parse as a document at all.">
                <cocoa key="pages"/>
            </property>
            <property name="dot commands" code="SRd3" type="text" list="yes" description="Dot commands observed, in file order.">
                <cocoa key="dotCommands"/>
            </property>
            <property name="unknown codes" code="SRd4" type="integer" description="Total occurrences of codes the parser did not recognize.">
                <cocoa key="unknownCodes"/>
            </property>
            <property name="comments present" code="SRd5" type="boolean" description="Whether the file carries any WordStar comments.">
                <cocoa key="commentsPresent"/>
            </property>
            <property name="margins" code="SRd6" type="page settings" description="The file's own resolved page geometry.">
                <cocoa key="margins"/>
            </property>
        </record-type>

        <!-- ================================= Classes ================================= -->

        <class-extension extends="document" description="A Soft Return document window.">
            <cocoa class="SoftReturn.WSDocument"/>

            <property name="variant" code="SRDv" type="variant"
                      description="Reading returns the currently-parsed variant (detected, or last forced). Setting re-parses the document under the new variant — the CLI's --force.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingVariant"/>
            </property>
            <property name="style" code="SRDs" type="style" description="The viewer's display mode. Reading reports exactly what the window shows, including native (job 313B — superseded the earlier printed-only reporting). Setting native switches the view the same way the View menu's Native item does.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingStyle"/>
            </property>
            <property name="page count" code="SRDc" type="integer" access="r" description="How many pages this document laid out, at its current style.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingPageCount"/>
            </property>
            <property name="current page" code="SRDp" type="integer" description="Which page is showing — the Go menu, as a property.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingCurrentPage"/>
            </property>
            <property name="zoom" code="SRDz" description="Fit, Actual Size, or a percentage number.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingZoom"/>
                <type type="zoom setting"/>
                <type type="real"/>
            </property>
            <property name="page size" code="SRDg" type="page size" description="The printed sheet override.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingPageSize"/>
            </property>
            <property name="modern font" code="SRDf" type="text" description="Modern style's typeface. Printed style ignores this — it is always Courier.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingModernFont"/>
            </property>
            <property name="modern size" code="SRDe" type="real" description="Modern style's point size. Printed style ignores this.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingModernSize"/>
            </property>
            <property name="show invisibles" code="SRDi" type="boolean" description="View ▸ Show Invisibles.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingShowInvisibles"/>
            </property>
            <!-- Job 254 (export-specifier): dispatch for the Soft Return Suite's own
                 "export" command — see that command's own comment and `ExportCommand`'s
                 header for why this class-extension, not a <cocoa class>, is where it's
                 bound. -->
            <responds-to command="export">
                <cocoa method="handleExportScriptCommand:"/>
            </responds-to>
        </class-extension>

        <!-- ================================= Commands ================================= -->

        <command name="export" code="SRsuexpo"
                 description="Export one document to one output file — the CLI's single-file conversion.">
            <!-- Job 254 (export-specifier): no <cocoa class> binding here, deliberately —
                 dispatch goes through the document class's <responds-to> below
                 (handleExportScriptCommand:), the same receiver-resolution mechanism
                 close/save already use, not a custom NSScriptCommand subclass. Candidate A
                 (resolving the specifier by hand inside a custom command's
                 performDefaultImplementation) did not fix job 252's field probe; this did. -->
            <direct-parameter type="specifier" description="The document to export."/>
            <parameter name="to" code="SRto" type="file" description="The output file's location.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingDestination"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="as" code="SRas" type="export format" description="The output format.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingFormat"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="using style" code="SRus" type="style" optional="yes"
                      description="Omitted: the document's current style.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingStyle"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="footnotes" code="SRbf" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="With/without footnotes in the output. Default: with.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingFootnotes"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="endnotes" code="SRbe" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="With/without endnotes in the output. Default: with.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingEndnotes"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="annotations" code="SRba" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="With/without annotations in the output. Default: with.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingAnnotations"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="comments" code="SRbc" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="With/without WordStar comments in the output. Default: without.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingComments"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="note references" code="SRnf" type="note reference style" optional="yes"
                      description="How note reference marks are shown in Modern output. Default: word style.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingNoteReferences"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="page settings" code="SRps" optional="yes"
                      description="A named preset, or a page settings record (e.g. from import page settings).">
                <cocoa key="scriptingPageSettings"/>
                <type type="settings preset"/>
                <type type="page settings"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="headers" code="SReh" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 373: with/without headers, footers, and page numbers (paged formats only — RTF/PDF). Omitted: Settings' own default.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingHeaders"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="table of contents" code="SRet" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 373: with/without a compiled Table of Contents/Index section, from the document's own .tc/.ix entries. Omitted: Settings' own default.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingTOC"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="inline styling" code="SRei" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 373: with/without the author's own inline color and font-size changes (RTF/HTML only). Omitted: Settings' own default.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingInlineStyling"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="pictures" code="SRep" type="pictures mode" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 373: how .PIX image references are handled. Omitted: Settings' own default.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingPictures"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="line numbers" code="SRel" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 504: with/without the document's own `.l#` line-number gutter (paged formats only — RTF/PDF). Default: with (the CLI's --line-numbers default).">
                <cocoa key="scriptingLineNumbers"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="styles" code="SRes" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 504: with/without the document's own paragraph styles passed through to formats that can carry them (HTML classes/CSS, RTF \stylesheet). Default: with; false is the CLI's --no-styles.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingStyles"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="fonts" code="SRef" type="fonts" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 504: which importer the RTF font names are chosen for (RTF only). Default: mac — the CLI's own D7 ruling, no longer this app's hardcoded ceiling.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingFontsTarget"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="page numbers" code="SRen" type="page numbers mode" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 506 (b31), updated job 520 (N5): WordStar's own AUTOMATIC page number (paged formats only — RTF/PDF). Omitted: Settings' own default.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingPageNumbers"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="sentence spacing" code="SRey" type="sentence spacing mode" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 521 (N9, b33): the typewriter double space after a sentence-ending . ? or ! (every format). Omitted: auto — there is deliberately no Settings default for this one.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingSentenceSpacing"/>
            </parameter>
            <result type="file" description="The file actually written — job 504: never the requested destination if that name already existed. A collision writes Finder-style, 'NAME 2.ext' (then 'NAME 3.ext', ...), never a silent overwrite; this is the name the result reports."/>
        </command>

        <command name="convert" code="SRsuconv"
                 description="Batch-convert files and/or folders, app-level, no windows — the CLI's -d.">
            <cocoa class="SoftReturn.ConvertCommand"/>
            <direct-parameter type="file" list="yes" description="Files and/or folders to convert."/>
            <parameter name="to folder" code="SRcf" type="file" optional="yes"
                      description="Omitted: each output lands beside its source.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingDestinationFolder"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="as" code="SRcy" type="export format" list="yes" description="The output format(s).">
                <cocoa key="scriptingFormats"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="using style" code="SRcs" type="style" optional="yes"
                      description="Omitted: each document's current/detected style.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingStyle"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="footnotes" code="SRkf" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 504: with/without footnotes in the output. Default: with.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingFootnotes"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="endnotes" code="SRke" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 504: with/without endnotes in the output. Default: with.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingEndnotes"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="annotations" code="SRka" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 504: with/without annotations in the output. Default: with.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingAnnotations"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="comments" code="SRkc" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 504: with/without WordStar comments in the output. Default: without.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingComments"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="searching subfolders" code="SRcb" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="With/without recursing into subfolders. Default: without.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingSearchingSubfolders"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="forcing variant" code="SRcv" type="variant" optional="yes"
                      description="Force every input to parse as this variant, for stubborn files.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingForcingVariant"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="page settings" code="SRcp" optional="yes"
                      description="A named preset, or a page settings record.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingPageSettings"/>
                <type type="settings preset"/>
                <type type="page settings"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="headers" code="SRch" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 373: with/without headers, footers, and page numbers (paged formats only — RTF/PDF). Omitted: Settings' own default.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingHeaders"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="table of contents" code="SRct" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 373: with/without a compiled Table of Contents/Index section, from each document's own .tc/.ix entries. Omitted: Settings' own default.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingTOC"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="inline styling" code="SRci" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 373: with/without the author's own inline color and font-size changes (RTF/HTML only). Omitted: Settings' own default.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingInlineStyling"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="pictures" code="SRcz" type="pictures mode" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 373: how .PIX image references are handled. Omitted: Settings' own default.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingPictures"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="line numbers" code="SRcl" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 504: with/without the document's own `.l#` line-number gutter (paged formats only — RTF/PDF). Default: with (the CLI's --line-numbers default).">
                <cocoa key="scriptingLineNumbers"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="styles" code="SRck" type="boolean" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 504: with/without each document's own paragraph styles passed through to formats that can carry them (HTML classes/CSS, RTF \stylesheet). Default: with; false is the CLI's --no-styles.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingStyles"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="fonts" code="SRcg" type="fonts" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 504: which importer the RTF font names are chosen for (RTF only). Default: mac — the CLI's own D7 ruling, no longer this app's hardcoded ceiling.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingFontsTarget"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="page numbers" code="SRcn" type="page numbers mode" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 506 (b31), updated job 520 (N5): WordStar's own AUTOMATIC page number (paged formats only — RTF/PDF). Omitted: Settings' own default.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingPageNumbers"/>
            </parameter>
            <parameter name="sentence spacing" code="SRcw" type="sentence spacing mode" optional="yes"
                      description="Job 521 (N9, b33): the typewriter double space after a sentence-ending . ? or ! (every format). Omitted: auto — there is deliberately no Settings default for this one.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingSentenceSpacing"/>
            </parameter>
            <result type="text" description="The output files' POSIX paths, one per line, in the order they were produced — job 504: the paths actually written, never a silent overwrite (a collision writes Finder-style, 'NAME 2.ext', 'NAME 3.ext', ...). Job 241's A/B matrix proved Cocoa Scripting's reply-packaging trampoline cannot coerce ANY list-shaped return value (native [NSURL] or a hand-built typeAEList, declared list=&quot;yes&quot; or not) into a real reply — every list-shaped variant returned errAEEventNotHandled (-1708) with a genuinely empty reply, while every SCALAR shape (text, a single file, or nil) succeeded. A scalar text blob is the only shape that both works and preserves every produced file's path for a batch of more than one; parse it by splitting on newlines. Empty is impossible: convert raises a script error instead when nothing converts (all inputs skipped or failed) — a partial run returns just the files it produced."/>
        </command>

        <command name="diagnose" code="SRsudiag"
                 description="Report what a file IS — the CLI's --diagnose, as JSON text (job 216: was a record; see docs/AppleScript-Dictionary.md for why).">
            <cocoa class="SoftReturn.DiagnoseCommand"/>
            <direct-parameter type="file" description="The file to inspect."/>
            <result type="text" description="Exactly sr --diagnose's own JSON rendering: keys sorted, two-space indent."/>
        </command>

        <command name="import page settings" code="SRsuimpg"
                 description="Read a WSCHANGE .PAT dump's page geometry — the CLI's --page-settings preset resolver, for an arbitrary machine's own patch file.">
            <cocoa class="SoftReturn.ImportPageSettingsCommand"/>
            <parameter name="from" code="SRpf" type="file" description="A .PAT file.">
                <cocoa key="scriptingSource"/>
            </parameter>
            <result type="text" description="JSON text (job 216: was a page settings record) with only the fields the .PAT dump actually set — mt_lines/mb_lines/po_cols/hm_lines/fm_lines/pl_lines, the same keys diagnose's own margins field uses. Cannot be fed directly back into another command's page settings parameter the way the old record result could; see docs/AppleScript-Dictionary.md."/>
        </command>

    </suite>
</dictionary>
